      "transcriber_notes": [
        "One row per day of the Western month; blank cells where a month has fewer days. Western cells give date and weekday as printed (M., T., W., Th., F., S., Sun.); Chinese cells give the day of the moon.",
        "Moon changes are printed as italic sub-headings inside the Chinese column: '12th Moon' before Jan 19 (1); '1st Moon' before Feb 18, whose Chinese cell is printed as the bracketed words 'Chinese New Year's Day' instead of a figure; '2nd Moon' before Mar 19 (1); '3rd Moon' before Apr 17 (1). Further moon sub-headings: '4th Moon' before May 17 (1); '5th Moon' before June 15 (1); '6th Moon' before July 14 (1); '7th Moon' before Aug 13 (1); '8th Moon' before Sept 11 (1); '9th Moon' before Oct 10 (1); '10th Moon' before Nov 9 (1); '11th Moon' before Dec 9 (1).",
        "Printed as one table per page with separate column headings; one part per page. Pages have no totals."
      ],
